Environment: FerretDB 2.5.0 + postgres-documentdb + NATS 2.11.4 ONLY. Every other dev-stack
container stopped. beanie 2.2.0, mongoengine 0.29.3, Python 3.13.13, 20-core Windows host.
"timed out after 5.0s" logger lines from NCRequester are filtered from the tables below; the
`t/out` column carries the count.


=========================================================================================
RUN 1 -- THE WRONG HARNESS, kept because it is the pre-registered failure mode
=========================================================================================
Saturator: ~400 small document writes/second, standing in for EventPersister.

variant          conc    ok  t/out  err   p50 ms   p95 ms   p99 ms  writes
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
raw                 1     1      0    0       36       36       36     395
raw                10    10      0    0       39       40       40     408
to_thread_part      1     1      0    0       22       22       22     458
to_thread_part     10    10      0    0       32       35       35     479
to_thread_full      1     1      0    0       33       33       33     413
to_thread_full     10    10      0    0       22       27       27     315
beanie              1     1      0    0       11       11       11     347
beanie             10    10      0    0       15       19       19     453

The `raw` CONTROL showed no starvation, which is the pre-registered "the harness is not
reproducing the symptom" outcome. Cause: many small writes do not starve a loop. The source
comment at persisted_agent_event_entity.py:584 names the real culprit -- "a 123s cold read of
30 days off disk". The saturator was rebuilt around ONE SLOW READ.


=========================================================================================
CALIBRATION -- how much corpus makes a FerretDB aggregation slow
=========================================================================================
   5000 docs | seed   0.11s | aggregate  0.061s (then 0.068s, 0.067s) | 50 rows
  20000 docs | seed   0.48s | aggregate  0.377s (then 0.371s, 0.314s) | 50 rows
  50000 docs | seed   1.19s | aggregate  0.772s (then 0.747s, 0.843s) | 50 rows
(FerretDB caps a write batch at 25000 operations.)


=========================================================================================
DIAGNOSTIC -- why to_thread_part looked WORSE than raw
=========================================================================================
=== raw ===
    client round-trip      :     1380 ms
    queued before handler  :     1071 ms
    lookup inside handler  :       35 ms

=== to_thread ===
    client round-trip      :     1834 ms
    queued before handler  :     1014 ms
    lookup inside handler  :      516 ms

Both wait ~1s for the loop. The difference is AFTER the handler is entered: to_thread needs a
SECOND loop slice to resume once the worker thread finishes, and on a contended loop that is
another blocking cycle. Real mechanism, not a harness artifact.


